# No energy/force/stress accuracy metric is reported in a form the schema captures (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - No MAE/RMSE/R2 metrics: accuracy is reported as the total-energy error and the RMSD of single relaxed structures in larger test supercells (e.g. 0.216 eV for the 323-atom SiO2 V_O2+ supercell, Defect-Only set III), in the text and Figs. 1-4. These single-structure errors are not encoded.
# - Smaller incremental training sets (I-III) of Tables II-IV are not separate runs. The maximum of 100,000 epochs is a cap with early stopping, so no epoch count is encoded. Train/validation splits: 8.5:1.5 (SiO2, Cu2ZnSnS4), 8:2 (GaN).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/dai2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
